    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“You’re an ENFP?! I’m an ENFP, too!” You may have heard a conversation like this. It’s all about the Myers-Briggs Type Indicator (MBTI) "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "personality test",
            "zh": "性格测试"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". You’ve probably seen it online and maybe you’ve taken a free test yourself."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The MBTI personality test uses four pairs of letters to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "group",
            "ref": "v-group"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " people into 16 personality types. These letter pairs are:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "l1",
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "E/I: where you get energy—being with people (E) vs. being alone (I)"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "S/N: how you take in "
            },
            {
              "t": "vocab",
              "v": "information",
              "ref": "v-information"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "—details (S) vs. big ideas (N)"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "T/F: how you make decisions—"
            },
            {
              "t": "gloss",
              "v": "logic",
              "zh": "逻辑"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " (T) vs. feelings (F)"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "J/P: how you deal with plans—"
            },
            {
              "t": "vocab",
              "v": "organized",
              "ref": "v-organized"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " (J) vs. "
            },
            {
              "t": "vocab",
              "v": "go with the flow",
              "ref": "v-go-with-the-flow"
            },
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": " (P)"
            }
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "You answer questions about how you think, feel, and act. After that, you’ll get a four-letter “type”, like ENFP or ISTJ."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "MBTI is "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "popular",
            "ref": "v-popular"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " because it’s quick, easy, and fun. People often use it as an "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "icebreaker",
            "zh": "破冰方式"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to talk about themselves. Friends talk and joke about their types. Some companies even use it when they’re "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "hiring",
            "zh": "聘用"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " people."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But MBTI has a bad side, too. It "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "labels",
            "zh": "贴标签"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " us. Once someone has a type, others may start to see them only through those four letters. For example, an “I-person” may be seen as quiet all the time. People may even use the label as an excuse. They might think, "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "I’m a “P”, so I cannot make good plans."
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Then, they won’t even try."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Four letters can’t "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "sum up",
            "ref": "v-sum-up"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a whole person. MBTI can help you learn about yourself, but don’t let it "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "box you in",
            "zh": "束缚"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". People grow and change all the time. An “F-person” can have logical thinking, and an “I-person” can still speak up. What matters most is not your type but your effort and choices."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
